<title>USA: Neff favors Delta, sees FY 97 EPS $10-$12 - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Neff favors Delta, sees FY 97 EPS $10-$12 - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment advisor John Neff favors Delta Air Lines Inc, and expects the company to earn between $10 and $12 per share for fiscal year 1997, Barron's financial weekly reported in its January 13 issue.</p>
<p>In Barron's 1997 investor roundatable, Neff said Delta has cut costs in recent years, negotiated a favorable contract with its pilots and maintained its fleet well.</p>
<p>His other stock picks included Owens Corning, Continental Homes Holding Corp, Reynolds Metals Co, Lyondell Petrochemical Co and Champion International Corp.</p>
</text>
